solution:
Since $\sin \alpha = \frac{7}{25}$, we have $\cos \alpha = \sqrt{1-\sin^2 \alpha} = \frac{24}{25}$. 

Since $\angle RPQ$ and $\angle RPS$ are supplementary angles, we have $\angle RPS = 180^\circ - \alpha$. 

