Let \[f(n) =
\begin{cases}
n^2-1 & \text{ if }n < 4,
\\ 3n-2 & \text{ if }n \geq 4.
\end{cases}
\]Find $f(f(f(2)))$.

solution:
Using the identity $\sec^2 x - \tan^2 x = 1,$ we can rewrite the given equation as $(\sec x - \tan x)(\sec x + \tan x) = \left(\frac{5}{2}\right)(1).$
Hence, $\sec x - \tan x = \boxed{\frac{2}{5}}.$
The answer is \frac{2}{5}

