solution:
Let $\overline{BD}$ be an altitude of the isosceles $\triangle ABC$, and let $O$ denote the center of the  circle with radius $r$ that passes through $A$, $B$, and $C$, as shown.

[asy]
pair O,A,C,B,D;
O=(0,0);
A=(-12,-16); C=(12,-16);
D=(0,-16); B=(0,20);
