solution:
Recall the cosine angle subtraction identity: $\cos (A - B) = \cos A \cos B + \sin A \sin B$.
Using this identity, we have
\begin{align*}
\cos 36^\circ - \cos 72^\circ &= \cos (72^\circ - 36^\circ) \\
&= \cos 36^\circ \cos 36^\circ + \sin 36^\circ \sin 36^\circ \\
&= (\cos 36^\circ)^2 + (\sin 36^\circ)^2 \\
&= \boxed{\frac{1}{2}}.
\end{align*}
The answer is \frac{1}{2}

