\[(1 - \cos \theta)(1 - \cos \theta) = \left( 1 - \frac{31}{32} \right) \left( 1 - \frac{1}{2} \right) = \frac{1}{32} \cdot \frac{1}{2} = \boxed{\frac{1}{64}}.\]The answer is \frac{1}{64}

